I hope to use distance sampling at point counts to estimate the density o=
f
2=963 species of small songbirds. I understand that counting the same
individual bird twice during a count at one point would inflate the densi=
ty
estimate. What I am wondering is whether counting the same bird from two
separate points creates any problem. I would like to use randomly selecte=
d
points, but if two or more fall near one another by chance, then counting
the same bird twice is definitely possible.  Do I need to design the surv=
ey
to avoid this?

